# What Vercel serves is this repository as it stands: the marketing site at
# the root, the app under /app, the shared rules the browser imports, and
# one function in /api. These have no business being downloadable.
#
# server/ is the migration and seed scripts. They run against the database
# from a checkout — `npm run migrate && npm run seed` — not from the
# deployment, so they are left out rather than published.
node_modules/
server/
.env
.env.example
